from pydantic import BaseModel, TypeAdapter", "explanation": "parse_obj_as is deprecated in Pydantic v2; TypeAdapter is the replacement. Literal is added for the const replacement, and Field is removed because it is no longer used after the const fields are converted."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/events.py:7:field-kwargs"], "search": "    type: str = Field("click", const=True)", "replace": "    type: Literal["click"] = "click"", "explanation": "The const=True keyword was removed in Pydantic v2. Per the migration guidance, use typing.Literal to fix the value, keeping "click" as the default."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/events.py:13:field-kwargs"], "search": "    type: str = Field("scroll", const=True)", "replace": "    type: Literal["scroll"] = "scroll"", "explanation": "The const=True keyword was removed in Pydantic v2. Per the migration guidance, use typing.Literal to fix the value, keeping "scroll" as the default."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/events.py:21:parse-obj-as"], "search": "        return parse_obj_as(List[Event], raw)", "replace": "        return TypeAdapter(List[Event]).validate_python(raw)", "explanation": "parse_obj_as is deprecated in Pydantic v2. Use TypeAdapter(T).validate_python(data) instead, as the finding specifies."}], "notes": "Four edits address all four findings. The import edit covers finding 3 and also swaps in Literal and TypeAdapter. Field is dropped from the import because nothing uses it after the const fields change. Event-model behavior is preserved: the defaults are unchanged and Literal enforces the same fixed value that const did. Note: the parse_events search string has 8 leading spaces to match the indented return line in the function body; the file content shows it at that indentation. No Pydantic model class beyond Click and Scroll is affected."}
